  "description": "Omni-Changeling's copy is every creature type, and so is a token copy of it (CR 604.3a)",
  "note": "An ability acquired through a copy effect is characteristic-defining (CR 604.3a). Omni-Changeling enters as a copy of bob's Goblin Piker except it has changeling; the copy's own printed changeling is gone (CR 707.2), so the exception is the only source of it. Lord of Atlantis reads it: a copy that is every creature type (CR 702.73a) is a Merfolk and gets +1/+1. Two controls on the one board stay 2/1: the Piker, and a Clone copying it without the exception. The Cackling Counterpart token copy is where the CDA claim bites: CR 707.2 copies the copiable values and leaves every CR 613 layer behind, so a changeling granted over the copy would make a 2/1 token. The Subtypes check is every creature type and no land type (CR 205.3m).",
